/-!
# The inductive step of the pseudo-coherence of an invertible object, on a ringed site

Let `(C, O)` be a ringed site and let `M` be an invertible object of `D(O)`. This file proves
the inductive step of the last paragraph of the source's proof of the first assertion of
Stacks 0FPV, for invertible `M`: if `M` is `m`-pseudo-coherent, then it is
`(m - 1)`-pseudo-coherent.

## The argument

Over the members of a covering there is a strictly perfect `ℰ`, vanishing below `m`, with a map
`ℰ ⟶ M` invertible on cohomology above `m` and onto in degree `m`. Complete it to a
distinguished triangle `ℰ ⟶ M ⟶ L ⟶ ℰ[1]`; then `L` has no cohomology in degrees `≥ m`, so it is
represented by a bounded above complex of flat modules `ℒ` vanishing in degrees `≥ m`, and `M` by
the splice `ℳ : … ⟶ ℒ^{m-2} ⟶ ℒ^{m-1} ⟶ ℰ^m ⟶ ℰ^{m+1} ⟶ …`, which is K-flat. Let `𝒩` be a
K-flat representative of the inverse of `M`. Over the members `W` of a further covering the
inverse of `Tot(ℳ ⊗ 𝒩) ≅ O[0]` is the class of a cocycle section `∑ fᵢ ⊗ gᵢ` over `W`; on the
localized site `C/W` the subcomplex `𝒦 ⊆ ℳ|_W` generated by `ℰ|_W` and the `fᵢ` is
`(m - 1)`-pseudo-coherent and `M|_W` is a retract of it, hence `(m - 1)`-pseudo-coherent by
Stacks 08FW. The conclusion is local, Stacks 08FU (3).

## Main results

* `DerivedCategory.isZero_homology_obj₃_of_triangle`: the vanishing of the cohomology of `L`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.InvertibleDerived.exists_kFlat_splice`: the splice
  representative.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.InvertibleDerived.isPseudoCoherentFrom_sub_one_of_approximation`:
  the conclusion over a site, given the approximation `ℰ ⟶ M` on the whole site.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FPV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FPV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FPY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FPY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08FU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08FU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08FW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08FW)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

